# Velantrim Titan 9.0 — Docker build context exclusions
#
# Goal: keep the build context small and make sure nothing from source
# control, local secrets, caches, or runtime-generated data ever reaches
# the Docker daemon (and therefore can never end up in an image layer).
#
# The Dockerfile does NOT use `COPY . .` — it copies only the explicit
# runtime assets it needs. This file is still authoritative because it
# governs the entire build context, including any wildcard COPY of a
# directory (e.g. `COPY core ./core` must not accidentally pick up a
# stray __pycache__/.env dropped inside core/).

# --- Version control ---
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Secrets / credentials ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/*.env
!config/*.example.env
# core/deployment_profiles.py's "developer" profile reads this one at
# runtime (VELANTRIM_PROFILE=developer) — see Dockerfile COPY.
!config/exocortex-dev.env
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# --- Python virtualenvs / caches ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# --- Build artifacts ---
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Runtime data / generated artifacts (not needed to build or run) ---
# Local databases are created fresh at container startup under /app/data
# (see docker-compose.yml volumes); none of the checked-in sample/dev DBs
# or the generated knowledge-graph export belong in the image.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
kb_graph.json

# --- Not needed to run the server ---
tests/
benchmarks/
node_modules/

# docs/ is excluded wholesale EXCEPT the three files api/web_console.py
# actually serves at runtime (/console/help, /console/research-mode.md,
# /console/research-roadmap.md). Excluding docs/* (rather than docs/)
# keeps the negations below working — a directory-level "docs/" match
# would shadow them (Docker does not descend into an excluded directory
# to re-include files inside it).
docs/*
!docs/CONSOLE_BROWSER_TEST.ru.md
!docs/RESEARCH_MODE.ru.md
!docs/EITI_PWA_RESEARCH_ROADMAP.ru.md
# core/umwelt_store.py's default seed (auto-loaded at startup when
# ENABLE_UMWELT_STORE + ENABLE_UMWELT_AUTO_SEED are on, both default "1").
# A file negation alone can't reach into an already-excluded directory
# (docs/seed matched "docs/*" above), so the directory itself must be
# re-included first, then re-excluded one level down, then the one file
# re-included again — the standard "allowlist one nested file" pattern.
!docs/seed
docs/seed/*
!docs/seed/umwelt_mvp_seed.json

# --- IDE / OS cruft ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Misc project temp/log artifacts ---
.claude/
.audit_tmp_*/
logs/
*.log
tmp_*
*-last.txt
*_last.txt
